        <h1 class="hero-title" style="color: #ffaa00;">Service Suspension: ETVaultGuard Lifecycle Update</h1>

        <div class="verse-box text-start" style="max-width: 100%; color: #ddd;">
            <h2 style="color: #00bfff;">Internal Code Review & Advisory</h2>
            <p>
                Following a rigorous internal security audit of the core codebase, a critical vulnerability was identified within the application's implementation framework. 
            </p>
            <p>
                To maintain data sovereignty and preserve cryptographic absolute security integrity for all platform deployment environments, remediating this issue requires a major, structural rewrite of the foundational logic layer—specifically focusing on hardware-level integration with the <strong>Trusted Platform Module (TPM)</strong>.
            </p>
            
            <blockquote>
                <strong>Vulnerability Mitigation Protocol:</strong> Until the cryptographic architectural revisions are fully finalized, vetted, and thoroughly tested, licensing distribution and system procurement windows are completely paused.
            </blockquote>

            <hr style="border-color: rgba(0, 191, 255, 0.3); margin: 2rem 0;" />

            <h2 style="color: #00bfff;">Infrastructure Changes & Timeline</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Production Site Offline:</strong> Effective <strong>May 10th</strong>, the standalone application storefront was detached from the perimeter gateway routing engines to mitigate attack vectors.</li>
                <li><strong>Dynamic Host Allocation:</strong> The supporting database node (<code>database.server.england</code>) has transitioned to an on-demand power management profile to save power and utility costs during active codebase refactoring blocks.</li>
            </ul>

            <hr style="border-color: rgba(0, 191, 255, 0.3); margin: 2rem 0;" />

            <h2 style="color: #00bfff;">Development Tracking & Open Source Parity</h2>
            <p>
                All development pipelines, component patch notes, and core architecture updates regarding the rewrite lifecycle are actively committed to the public open-source repository mirror:
            </p>
            
            <div class="mt-3">
                <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/awesomeshot5051/ETVaultGuard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" 
                   style="background: rgba(0, 191, 255, 0.1); border: 1px solid #00bfff; color: #fff !important; font-family: 'Cascadia Code', monospace; padding: 10px 20px; transition: all 0.2s ease;">
                    GitHub Mirror: awesomeshot5051/ETVaultGuard ↗
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
